  "confidence": "medium",
  "note": "the upper rocker (21-23) and the small button 20 are on the part of the face turned away and show only in silhouette at the right edge. The rear-side controls (24 upper rear button, 44 lower rear button) are on the side turned away; 19 (head pad) and 43 (under the red CHOP cover, per the sheet's side drawing) are not identifiable. The two small round things on the left side below the head are screws of a side plate, not controls. second actions share their control: 45 = STOW/DEP toggle, 46 = button 35, 47 = button 43 (two-dot symbols on the sheet). The collective axis comes from the Rotor TCS base (marker on the grip handle); the throttle twist and the engine idle button (1) sit on the base tube, not in the photo.",
